  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nI am using Jellyseerr with Lidarr support (`fallenbagel/jellyseerr:preview-music-support`), and it seems that the Media Requests List widget is hardcoded for only 'movies' and 'tv', and fails when it encounters a music item.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Run Jellyseerr with Lidarr support\n2. Add that Jellyseerr instance as an integration\n3. Add a Media Requests List widget to your dashboard with Jellyseerr instance as the integration source\n4. Observe the `TRPCClientError: Failed to parse integration data` error message on the widget\n\n### Impact\n\nThe Media Requests List widget is completely unusable for me.\n\n### Additional information\n\nLogs: \n[homarr.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23868722/homarr.log)\n\nError message:\n<img width=\"454\" height=\"223\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5698d45c-a2a2-4e9e-839d-668c193b5169\" />\n\n### Version\n\n1.45.0\n\n### Installation method\n\nDocker Compose\n\n### Browser\n\nFirefox",
